.TH AKIRA 1 "2026-11-05" "unheaded 6fd704da" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
akira \- Kingdom health daemon: polls every service, publishes votes to Wotan and decides the health band by consensus (ADR\-029).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B akira
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kingdom health daemon: polls every service, publishes votes to Wotan and decides the health band by consensus (ADR\-029).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fISTRING\fR
Path to config YAML (optional)
.TP
.B \-\-node \fISTRING\fR
Node identifier (default: hostname)
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run single health sweep and exit
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIN\fR
HTTP API port for Akira status (default 19100)
.TP
.B \-\-pprof \fIADDR\fR
serve net/http/pprof on this loopback ADDR (e.g. 127.0.0.1:6060); off when empty
.TP
.B \-\-remediate
restart a service in this node's own targets (systemctl restart unheaded\-<name>) when two\-thirds of reporters see it failing; off by default
.TP
.B \-\-wotan \fISTRING\fR
Wotan HTTP address for publishing health reports (default http://localhost:18000)
.TP
.B \-\-wotan\-grpc \fISTRING\fR
Wotan gRPC address for the signed topics (consensus, remediate); default: the \-\-wotan host on port 18001
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
akira
akira \-\-once
akira \-\-config /etc/unheaded/akira.yaml
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
